; facetec-api default scan acceptance rules — SPOCP advanced format
; Each rule must be on a single line. Atoms are unquoted.
;
; Numeric thresholds are encoded as SPOCP range predicates (* range numeric ...).
; Liveness scores are 3-digit zero-padded integers (000-100).
; Face match levels are 2-digit zero-padded integers (00-10).
;
; Field order: liveness-score, face-match-level, doc-type, mrz-verified,
;              nfc-verified, barcode-verified, chip-trusted
; Rules may stop at any field — trailing query fields beyond the rule are ignored.
;
; chip-trusted is true only when facetec-api itself verified the eMRTD chip
; (SOD signature + data-group hashes + DG1/MRZ cross-check) AND the go-trust PDP
; says the document signer chains to a reviewed CSCA for the issuing state.
; It is independent of nfc-verified, which is only FaceTec's own chip check
; (hashes vs. the DSC embedded in the same chip -- integrity, not authenticity).
; Positional matching means a rule that constrains chip-trusted must also list
; the fields before it; (* set true false) matches either value.
;
; FaceTec nfcAuthenticationStatusEnumInt 3 (FAILED) and 5 (FAILED_DUE_TO_SIGNATURE_
; VERIFICATION) are rejected in code regardless of these rules. Status 1
; (NOT_SUPPORTED_BY_DOCUMENT: no Active/Chip Authentication on the chip) is
; permitted, but it is a weaker clone-detection signal; it is recorded in the
; audit log (chip_auth_status) so that it can be reviewed afterwards.
;
; Default thresholds: liveness >= 80, face-match >= 06.
; To tighten or relax thresholds per deployment, edit these rules directly.

; Accept passports with MRZ verification AND a chip whose document signer is trusted
(facetec-scan (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 080)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 06)) (doc-type passport) (mrz-verified true) (nfc-verified (* set true false)) (barcode-verified (* set true false)) (chip-trusted true))
; Relaxed variant (NOT recommended; no CSCA validation of the chip). Only for
; deployments without a go-trust PDP (set trust.required: false). To use it,
; comment out the rule above and uncomment this one:
; (facetec-scan (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 080)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 06)) (doc-type passport) (mrz-verified true))
; Accept driving licences with barcode verification
(facetec-scan (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 080)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 06)) (doc-type dl) (mrz-verified false) (nfc-verified false) (barcode-verified true))
; Accept national ID cards
(facetec-scan (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 080)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 06)) (doc-type id_card))

; --- Operator review rules (ETSI 119 461 §4.5 escalation) ---
; NOTE: These rules use the "facetec-scan-review" head atom. The policy engine
; must query both "facetec-scan" (for accept/reject) and "facetec-scan-review"
; (for escalation) to enable the operator review path.
; Escalate borderline passports: liveness >= 60 AND face-match >= 4
; (entries that also satisfy the accept rules above will match accept first).
; A passport whose chip is not trusted must not be escalated for acceptance.
(facetec-scan-review (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 060)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 04)) (doc-type passport) (mrz-verified true) (nfc-verified (* set true false)) (barcode-verified (* set true false)) (chip-trusted true))
; Escalate borderline driving licences
(facetec-scan-review (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 060)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 04)) (doc-type dl) (barcode-verified true))
; Escalate borderline ID cards
(facetec-scan-review (liveness-score (* range numeric ge 060)) (face-match-level (* range numeric ge 04)) (doc-type id_card))
